<title>GERMANY: Buba allots 69 bln marks in tender at 3 pct.</title>
<headline>Buba allots 69 bln marks in tender at 3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank said it allocated 69 billion marks of securities repurchase funds at this week's tender at a fixed rate of three percent, the rate that has prevailed since late August.</p>
<p>A repo pact for 71.9 billion marks expires today, Wednesday, so a net 2.9 billion marks is draining from the market.</p>
<p>The Bundesbank said banks bid for 273.4 billion marks of the repurchase funds this week.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
